        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Said to have been used for \"Peter's pence\" -- money sent yearly to Rome. Linen completely covered with silk. Design: coat of arms surmounted by crown and canopy, surrounded by rococo foliage, worked in fine petit-point with pink yellow, green, blue, cream white, and a little black silk, with gold and silver thread, (several threads used together), on a neutral bluish violet ground. Back and front similar, bound with gold braid, a blue tasselled cord on top."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/8fbf2e86-2c27-34c9-bdb2-23fd1b4e4eb1> .

